Chapter: ParticleSpread
  cites Sim chapter ParticleSystem

 An emitter's three velocity components must be independent draws. They
 used to come from one hash read at s, s + 1000 and s + 2000, and since
 psys-noise takes a remainder, adding a constant to the hash added a
 constant to the answer: every particle got the same y minus x offset,
 and at a spread of 100 that offset was exactly zero.

 This reads the EMITTED particles rather than recomposing the helpers,
 which is the only way to measure what the emitter does. Recomposing
 them by hand is how the first version of this probe kept reporting the
 old behaviour after the fix had landed.

 A marginal histogram cannot see this and did not: the spread of vx
 alone was even both before and after. The measurement has to be joint.

Section: Emitting

  sys-for : Integer -> ParticleSystem
  sys-for (spread) =
    psys-emit (psys-new 400) (emitter-new 0 0 0 0 0 0 spread 100 0) 200 12345

  dy-at : ParticleSystem, Integer -> Integer
  dy-at (sys) (i) =
    let p = list-at (sys.particles) i
    in p.part-vy - p.part-vx

  share : ParticleSystem, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  share (sys) (target) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else share sys target (i + 1) n (acc + (if dy-at sys i == target then 1 else 0))

  modal : Integer -> Integer
  modal (spread) =
    let s = sys-for spread
    in share s (dy-at s 0) 0 200 0

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("emitted=" & show (psys-count (sys-for 100)))
    print-line-uni ("modal-dy-share-sp64=" & show (modal 64))
    print-line-uni ("modal-dy-share-sp100=" & show (modal 100))
    print-line-uni ("sample-dy=" & show (dy-at (sys-for 100) 0) & " " & show (dy-at (sys-for 100) 1) & " " & show (dy-at (sys-for 100) 2))
    print-line-uni ("independent=" & (if modal 100 < 20 then "yes" else "no"))
  end

